# Your regular command sequence

Every time you finish a meaningful change, use:

```powershell
git status
git add .
git status
git commit -m "Describe what you changed"
git push
git status
```

You do not technically need every `git status`, but while learning, this sequence is best because you can see each stage.

---

# Practical example: updating `Roadmap.md`

You open:

```text
Docs/Roadmap.md
```

You add:

```markdown
- [ ] Install ROS 2 Jazzy
- [ ] Create publisher and subscriber nodes
```

Save it, then run:

```powershell
